From a5bc4bfd0b6a05da8339731d7e5d662465af70a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluezr <bluezr@dogecoin.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:36:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] psbt: complete the finalizer and extractor roles for
 non-standard scripts

doc/psbt.md documents a six-role pipeline and a per-input map whose 0x07 entry
is "final scriptSig (set by the finalizer)". Two of those roles were only
usable for scripts the library recognises.

dogecoin_psbt_finalize_input() classifies the input and builds a scriptSig for
the shapes it knows. BIP174 leaves the finalizer application specific because a
redeem script can be anything, and a PSBT whose script did not classify could
not be completed: 0x07 is serialized but only the built-in finalizer could ever
set it. dogecoin_psbt_input_set_final_scriptsig() lets the caller supply one and
marks the input finalized. Correctness is the caller's, since nothing here can
check a scriptSig without knowing the script's semantics.

dogecoin_psbt_extract() returns a dogecoin_tx and tx.h is not installed, so a
consumer could produce the finalized transaction and had no way to serialize it
for broadcast; dogecoin_tx_deserialize() is public with no inverse.
dogecoin_psbt_extract_hex() closes that.

Both are declared in psbt.h as well as libdogecoin.h. Declaring only the latter
left the in-tree tests, which include psbt.h, with an implicit declaration:
extract_hex was assumed to return int, the pointer was truncated, and the test
segfaulted on a string it had just been handed.

test_psbt_custom_finalizer covers an unfinalized PSBT refusing both extractors,
a caller-supplied scriptSig reaching the extracted tx byte for byte, the hex
agreeing with it, replacement not appending, and NULL and out-of-range
rejections. It fails on 1447 with the setter stubbed and on 1463 with the hex
buffer left unfilled. 103/103.
